# =============================================================================
# NFTBan Bot Scanner - Custom User Patterns
# =============================================================================
# Add your custom patterns below. Format:
#
# NAME|PATTERN|MATCH_TYPE|THRESHOLD|WINDOW|BAN|ENABLED|DESCRIPTION
#
# MATCH_TYPE options:
#   url-404  = Match only if HTTP 404 response
#   url-any  = Match any HTTP response code
#   url-post = Match POST requests only
#   url-get  = Match GET requests only
#   path-404|path-any|path-get|path-post = the regex sees the request PATH only
#   distinct-404|distinct-any|distinct-get|distinct-post = each DISTINCT request
#              target counts once per IP (probing/enumeration)
#   useragent = Match the User-Agent
#
# This file is YOURS (v1.234+): packages never ship, replace or remove it.
# The shipped rules live in /usr/lib/nftban/data/botscan_*.patterns and are
# replaced on every upgrade. Do not copy them here: a record that reuses a
# shipped NAME is ignored. To change a shipped rule, disable it with
#   nftban botscan patterns disable NAME      (writes override.local)
# and add your own record below under a new name.
#
# Example:
# MY_PATTERN|malicious\.php|url-404|3|60|3600|true|My custom pattern
#
# =============================================================================

